From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 20:03:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/haswell: Route PCIe root port interrupts to PIRQA-D

The ACPI routing tables of the PCH root ports (IRQM() in
southbridge/intel/common/acpi/pcie.asl) assume that D28IR routes INTA
to INTD to PIRQA to PIRQD, and swizzle the pins of downstream devices
by root port number. For example, INTA of a device behind root port 2
is reported as GSI 17. The OEM firmware reports the same routing, e.g.
INTA behind EXP2 is GSI 17 and INTD is GSI 16.

These boards however route all four pins of device 28 to PIRQA, so the
hardware delivers every legacy interrupt from behind the root ports on
GSI 16. Devices behind root ports 2 to 4 that use INTx instead of MSI,
and devices using INTB to INTD behind root ports 1 and 5, do not get
their interrupts, e.g. an ath9k WiFi card, which uses INTx by default,
in the slot on root port 2.

Route the pins to PIRQA-D to match the ACPI tables.

TEST=Built for W541 and T440p. Not tested on hardware yet.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/romstage.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/romstage.c b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/romstage.c
index 64d8cd442..f786f68bf 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/romstage.c
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/romstage.c
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@ void mainboard_config_rcba(void)
 {
 	RCBA16(D31IR) = DIR_ROUTE(PIRQA, PIRQD, PIRQC, PIRQA);
 	RCBA16(D29IR) = DIR_ROUTE(PIRQH, PIRQD, PIRQA, PIRQC);
-	RCBA16(D28IR) = DIR_ROUTE(PIRQA, PIRQA, PIRQA, PIRQA);
+	RCBA16(D28IR) = DIR_ROUTE(PIRQA, PIRQB, PIRQC, PIRQD);
 	RCBA16(D27IR) = DIR_ROUTE(PIRQG, PIRQB, PIRQC, PIRQD);
 	RCBA16(D26IR) = DIR_ROUTE(PIRQA, PIRQF, PIRQC, PIRQD);
 	RCBA16(D25IR) = DIR_ROUTE(PIRQE, PIRQF, PIRQG, PIRQH);
